![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)

This function does not correctly handle the CPU-only case. If `is_mps_available` is `False`, `get_device_name()` will return `'cpu'`, and this function will raise a `RuntimeError`. To fully support CPU environments, you should add a check for the 'cpu' device and return the 'gloo' backend.

```suggestion
    elif is_mps_available:
        return "gloo"
    elif get_device_name() == "cpu":
        return "gloo"
    else:
        raise RuntimeError(f"No available nccl backend found on device type {get_device_name()}.")
```

